During the year, sales (net of trade discount) of Rs. 245,000 were made on credit.
Receipts from customers amounted to Rs. 210,200 and cash discounts of Rs. 700 were allowed. Refunds of Rs.
1,300 were made to customers.
What should be the closing balance at 31 May 2018 of account receivable account?', '["Rs. 64650","Rs. 68250","Rs. 66950","Rs. 67950"]', 1, '[]', false, 1, 'Opening Balance ($Rs. 32,850$): This is the starting amount owed by customers.
Credit Sales ($+ Rs. 245,000$): These increase the amount customers owe the business. Trade discounts are already deducted from the sales figure, so we use the net amount.
Receipts from Customers ($- Rs. 210,200$): This represents cash or cheques received, which reduces the outstanding debt.Cash Discounts Allowed ($- Rs. 700$): This is an incentive given to customers for early payment. It reduces their balance without a corresponding cash receipt.Refunds ($+ Rs. 1,300$): When a business refunds a customer (for example, if they overpaid), it increases the receivable balance again because the cash that previously reduced the balance is given back.Final Calculation:$$32,850 + 245,000 - 210,200 - 700 + 1,300 = 68,250$$The closing balance at 31 May 2018 is Rs. 68,250.', 'medium', 'cmlb6jtrf006doga3hpkyta6l', '2026-02-06T12:49:30.751Z', '2026-02-06T14:04:11.119Z', NULL, '[]');

