Plus: Amount Charged to P&L: 17,200
Total Closing Allowance: 35,200

Step 2: Isolate the General Allowance Amount
The total closing allowance (35,200) is composed of the specific allowance and the general allowance.
Total Closing Allowance: 35,200
Less: Specific Allowance: (16,000)
General Allowance (in Rupees): 19,200

Step 3: Calculate the General Allowance Percentage
The general allowance is calculated on the receivables after deducting the specific debt.
Find the Balance for General Allowance:
Total Receivables: 400,000
Less: Specific Debt: (16,000)
Balance Subject to General %: 384,000
Calculate the Percentage:
Percentage=(General Allowance Amount÷Balance for General Allowance)×100
Percentage=(19,200÷384,000)×100
