Net purchases = 253k - 8k = 245k
Step 2: Cost of goods available for sale
COGAS = 120k + 245k = 365k
Step 3: Calculate cost of sales
Markup 25% on cost means:

If cost = 100, selling price = 125
Cost = Sales / 1.25

Regular sales:
Sales (excluding special customer) = 285.25k - 35.25k = 250k
Cost = 250k / 1.25 = 200k
Special customer sales (6% discount):

Discounted price = 35.25k
Normal price before discount = 35.25k / 0.94 = 37.5k
Cost = 37.5k / 1.25 = 30k

Total cost of sales: 200k + 30k = 230k
Step 4: Adjust for damaged goods

Damaged goods sales value: 10k
Cost of damaged goods = 10k / 1.25 = 8k
Loss on damaged goods = 8k - 6k (insurance) = 2k
These goods are removed from inventory at cost: 8k

Step 5: Closing inventory
Closing inventory = 365k - 230k - 8k = 127k', 'hard', 'cmlavvqbm009gkoa3sx19b6ow', '2026-02-06T07:50:56.915Z', '2026-02-16T13:39:48.648Z', NULL, '[]');
